					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-307808#post-2485822</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-307808/decency#post-2485822</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 04 Apr 2016 16:52:02 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>rotze_emeth</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1513704</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Loved it.</p> <p>My headcanon for this is that the narrator &quot;passed&quot; the psych exams, i.e. actually has some sociopathic tendencies, but decided based on his ideas (not his bizarre feelings) about right and wrong that this potentially world-ending action is the right thing to do.</p> <p>i.e. He consciously decides that (one person knowing their humanity) == (whole world).</p> <p>IMO that's not a decision we see often enough. +1</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
